# Mirrors .gitignore's "regenerated on demand, not source" list, plus
# Docker-specific excludes. Keeping the build context small also keeps
# `docker build` from re-uploading multi-GB of local cache/venv state
# on every rebuild.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
env/

.git/
.github/

.cache/
.chroma/
vector_db/
filings_cache/
models/
narrative_comparison/
/reports/
llm_logs/
*.db

# Frontend, MLflow tracking data, and a local scratch data dir -- none
# of this backend-only image needs any of it, and each was silently
# bloating the build context by 500MB-1.5GB+ (confirmed live: web/'s
# node_modules alone is ~1.3GB, mlruns/ ~490MB), turning "load build
# context" into the slowest step of the whole build.
web/
mlruns/
Data_Comparison/

# Terraform IaC -- never needed inside the application image, and
# infra/terraform.tfvars (gitignored, never committed -- see
# infra/.gitignore) can hold real plaintext secrets for local runs.
# .gitignore keeps it out of the repo, but COPY . . doesn't consult
# .gitignore at all -- confirmed live via a real Trivy scan of a build
# from this directory: a local tfvars file's private key and API
# secrets ended up baked into the image layers. Excluding the whole
# directory here closes that regardless of what's gitignored.
infra/

scripts/finetuned_bge_embeddings/

.streamlit/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

.env
